and reverts to the\noriginal value when exiting the context.", "start_line": 394, "end_line": 399, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "modify_settings", "qualified_name": "modify_settings", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A context manager that temporarily applies changes to a list setting\nand reverts back to the original value when exiting the context.", "start_line": 401, "end_line": 406, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertRedirects", "qualified_name": "assertRedirects", "args": ["self", "response", "expected_url", "status_code", "target_status_code", "msg_prefix", "fetch_redirect_response"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that a response redirected to a specific URL and that the\nredirect URL can be loaded.\n\nWon't work for external links since it uses the test client to do a\nrequest (use fetch_redirect_response=False to check such links without\nfetching them).", "start_line": 408, "end_line": 525, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertURLEqual", "qualified_name": "assertURLEqual", "args": ["self", "url1", "url2", "msg_prefix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that two URLs are the same, ignoring the order of query string\nparameters except for parameters with the same name.\n\nFor example, /path/?x=1&y=2 is equal to /path/?y=2&x=1, but\n/path/?a=1&a=2 isn't equal to /path/?a=2&a=1.", "start_line": 527, "end_line": 549, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_text_repr", "qualified_name": "_text_repr", "args": ["self", "content", "force_string"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 551, "end_line": 554, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_assert_contains", "qualified_name": "_assert_contains", "args": ["self", "response", "text", "status_code", "msg_prefix", "html"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 556, "end_line": 594, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertContains", "qualified_name": "assertContains", "args": ["self", "response", "text", "count", "status_code", "msg_prefix", "html"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that a response indicates that some content was retrieved\nsuccessfully, (i.e., the HTTP status code was as expected) and that\n``text`` occurs ``count`` times in the content of the response.\nIf ``count`` is None, the count doesn't matter - the assertion is true\nif the text occurs at least once", "start_line": 596, "end_line": 628, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertNotContains", "qualified_name": "assertNotContains", "args": ["self", "response", "text", "status_code", "msg_prefix", "html"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that a response indicates that some content was retrieved\nsuccessfully, (i.e., the HTTP status code was as expected) and that\n``text`` doesn't occur in the content of the response.", "start_line": 630, "end_line": 647, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_check_test_client_response", "qualified_name": "_check_test_client_response", "args": ["self", "response", "attribute", "method_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Raise a ValueError if the given response doesn't have the required\nattribute.", "start_line": 649, "end_line": 658, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_form_repr", "qualified_name": "_form_repr", "args": ["self", "form", "formset", "form_index"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 660, "end_line": 663, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_assert_form_error", "qualified_name": "_assert_form_error", "args": ["self", "form", "field", "errors", "msg_prefix", "formset", "form_index"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 665, "end_line": 696, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertFormError", "qualified_name": "assertFormError", "args": ["self", "form", "field", "errors", "msg_prefix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that a field named \"field\" on the given form object has specific\nerrors.\n\nerrors can be either a single error message or a list of errors\nmessages. Using errors=[] test that the field has no errors.\n\nYou can pass field=None to check the form's non-field errors.", "start_line": 698, "end_line": 711, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertFormSetError", "qualified_name": "assertFormSetError", "args": ["self", "formset", "form_index", "field", "errors", "msg_prefix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Similar to assertFormError() but for formsets.\n\nUse form_index=None to check the formset's non-form errors (in that\ncase, you must also use field=None).\nOtherwise use an integer to check the formset's n-th form for errors.\n\nOther parameters are the same as assertFormError().", "start_line": 713, "end_line": 758, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_template_used", "qualified_name": "_get_template_used", "args": ["self", "response", "template_name", "msg_prefix", "method_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 760, "end_line": 778, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_assert_template_used", "qualified_name": "_assert_template_used", "args": ["self", "template_name", "template_names", "msg_prefix", "count"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 780, "end_line": 797, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertTemplateUsed", "qualified_name": "assertTemplateUsed", "args": ["self", "response", "template_name", "msg_prefix", "count"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that the template with the provided name was used in rendering\nthe response. Also usable as context manager.", "start_line": 799, "end_line": 818, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assertTemplateNotUsed", "qualified_name": "assertTemplateNotUsed", "args": ["self", "response", "template_name", "msg_prefix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Assert that the template with the provided name was NOT used in\nrendering the response. Also usable as context manager.", "st