ed yet.", "start_line": 129, "end_line": 138, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_models_ready", "qualified_name": "check_models_ready", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Raise an exception if all models haven't been imported yet.", "start_line": 140, "end_line": 143, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_app_configs", "qualified_name": "get_app_configs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Import applications and return an iterable of app configs.", "start_line": 145, "end_line": 148, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_app_config", "qualified_name": "get_app_config", "args": ["self", "app_label"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Import applications and returns an app config for the given label.\n\nRaise LookupError if no application exists with this label.", "start_line": 150, "end_line": 165, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_models", "qualified_name": "get_models", "args": ["self", "include_auto_created", "include_swapped"], "decorators": ["functools.cache"], "docstring": "Return a list of all installed models.\n\nBy default, the following models aren't included:\n\n- auto-created models for many-to-many relations without\n  an explicit intermediate table,\n- models that have been swapped out.\n\nSet the corresponding keyword argument to True to include such models.", "start_line": 169, "end_line": 186, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_model", "qualified_name": "get_model", "args": ["self", "app_label", "model_name", "require_ready"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the model matching the given app_label and model_name.\n\nAs a shortcut, app_label may be in the form <app_label>.<model_name>.\n\nmodel_name is case-insensitive.\n\nRaise LookupError if no application exists with this label, or no\nmodel exists with this name in the application. Raise ValueError if", "start_line": 188, "end_line": 213, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "register_model", "qualified_name": "register_model", "args": ["self", "app_label", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 215, "end_line": 240, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_installed", "qualified_name": "is_installed", "args": ["self", "app_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check whether an application with this name exists in the registry.\n\napp_name is the full name of the app e.g. 'django.contrib.admin'.", "start_line": 242, "end_line": 249, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_containing_app_config", "qualified_name": "get_containing_app_config", "args": ["self", "object_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Look for an app config containing a given object.\n\nobject_name is the dotted Python path to the object.\n\nReturn the app config for the inner application in case of nesting.\nReturn None if the object isn't in any registered app config.", "start_line": 251, "end_line": 268, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_registered_model", "qualified_name": "get_registered_model", "args": ["self", "app_label", "model_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Similar to get_model(), but doesn't require that an app exists with\nthe given app_label.\n\nIt's safe to call this method at import time, even while the registry\nis being populated.", "start_line": 270, "end_line": 281, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_swappable_settings_name", "qualified_name": "get_swappable_settings_name", "args": ["self", "to_string"], "decorators": ["functools.cache"], "docstring": "For a given model string (e.g. \"auth.User\"), return the name of the\ncorresponding settings name if it refers to a swappable model. If the\nreferred model is not swappable, return None.\n\nThis method is decorated with @functools.cache because it's performance\ncritical when it comes to migrations. Since", "start_line": 284, "end_line": 304, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_available_apps", "qualified_name": "set_available_apps", "args": ["self", "available"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Restrict the set of installed apps used by get_app_config[s].\n\navailable must be an iterable of application names.\n\nset_available_apps() must be balanced with unset_available_apps().\n\nPrimarily used for performance optimization in TransactionTestCase.\n\nThis method is safe in the sense that it doesn'", "start_line": 306, "end_line": 332, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unset_available_apps", "qualified_name": "unset_available_apps", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Cancel a previous call to set_available_apps().", "start_line": 334, "end_line": 337, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_installed_apps", "qualified_name": "set_installed_apps", "args": ["self", "installed"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Enable a different set of installed apps for get_app_config[s].\n\ninstalled must be an iterable in the same format as INSTALLED_APPS.\n\nset_installed_apps() must be balanced with unset_installed_apps(),\neven if it exits with an exception.\n\nPrimarily used as a receiver of the setting_changed signal in ", "start_line": 339, "end_line": 362, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unset_installed_apps", "qualified_name": "unset_installed_apps", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Cancel a previous call to set_installed_apps().", "start_line": 364, "end_line": 368, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_cache", "qualified_name": "clear_cache", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clear all internal caches, for methods that alter the app registry.\n\nThis is mostly used in tests.", "start_line": 370, "end_line": 386, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lazy_model_operation", "qualified_name": "lazy_model_operation", "args": ["self", "function"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Take a function and a number of (\"app_label\", \"modelname\") tuples, and\nwhen all the corresponding models have been imported and registered,\ncall the function with the model classes as its arguments.\n\nThe function passed to this method must accept exactly n models as\narguments, where n=len(model_keys", "start_line": 388, "end_line": 426, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "do_pending_operations", "qualified_name": "do_pending_operations", "args": ["self", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Take a newly-prepared model and pass it to each function waiting for\nit. This is called at the very end of Apps.register_model().", "start_line": 428, "end_line": 435, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "apply_next_model", "qualified_name": "apply_next_model", "args": ["model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 411, "end_line": 413, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Apps", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "populate", "check_apps_ready", "check_models_ready", "get_app_configs", "get_app_config", "get_models", "get_model", "register_model", "is_installed", "get_containing_app_config", "get_registered_model", "get_swappable_settings_name", "set_available_apps", "unset_available_apps", "set_installed_apps", "unset_installed_apps", "clear_cache", "lazy_model_operation", "do_pending_operations"], "docstring": "A registry that stores the configuration of installed applications.\n\nIt also keeps track of models, e.g. to provide reverse relations.", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 435}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "django/views/defaults.py", "file_hash": "0574f7e9abb0f17179670a9d5346a4cd7e484c505686ecbc89d4fc606902a3f2", "imports": [{"module": "urllib.parse", "names": ["quote"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "django.http", "names": ["HttpResponseBadRequest", "HttpResponseForbidden", "HttpResponseNotFound", "HttpResponseServerError"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "django.te