fe for (HTML) output purposes. The returned\nobject can be used everywhere a string is appropriate.\n\nIf used on a method as a decorator, mark the returned data as safe.\n\nCan be called multiple times on a single string.", "start_line": 65, "end_line": 78, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__html__", "qualified_name": "__html__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the html representation of a string for interoperability.\n\nThis allows other template engines to understand Django's SafeData.", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 22, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__add__", "qualified_name": "__add__", "args": ["self", "rhs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Concatenating a safe string with another safe bytestring or\nsafe string is safe. Otherwise, the result is no longer safe.", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 47, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__str__", "qualified_name": "__str__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 49, "end_line": 50, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "wrapper", "qualified_name": "wrapper", "args": [], "decorators": ["wraps(func)"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 58, "end_line": 59, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "SafeData", "bases": [], "methods": ["__html__"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 22}, {"name": "SafeString", "bases": ["str", "SafeData"], "methods": ["__add__", "__str__"], "docstring": "A str subclass that has been specifically marked as \"safe\" for HTML output\npurposes.", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 50}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Functions for working with \"safe strings\": strings that can be displayed safely\nwithout further escaping in HTML. Marking something as a \"safe string\" means\nthat the producer of the string has already turned characters that should not\nbe interpreted by the HTML engine (e.g. '<') into the appropriate entities.", "parse_error": ""}