in the\nquantifier.\n\nReturn the minimum number of occurrences permitted by the quantifier and\neither None or the next character from the input_iter if the next character\nis not part of the quantifier.", "start_line": 238, "end_line": 272, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "contains", "qualified_name": "contains", "args": ["source", "inst"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return True if the \"source\" contains an instance of \"inst\". False,\notherwise.", "start_line": 275, "end_line": 286, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "flatten_result", "qualified_name": "flatten_result", "args": ["source"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Turn the given source sequence into a list of reg-exp possibilities and\ntheir arguments. Return a list of strings and a list of argument lists.\nEach of the two lists will be of the same length.", "start_line": 289, "end_line": 340, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_lazy_re_compile", "qualified_name": "_lazy_re_compile", "args": ["regex", "flags"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Lazily compile a regex with flags.", "start_line": 343, "end_line": 354, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_compile", "qualified_name": "_compile", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 346, "end_line": 352, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Choice", "bases": ["list"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Represent multiple possibilities at this point in a pattern string.", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 31}, {"name": "Group", "bases": ["list"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Represent a capturing group in the pattern string.", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 35}, {"name": "NonCapture", "bases": ["list"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Represent a non-capturing group in the pattern string.", "start_line": 38, "end_line": 39}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Functions for reversing a regular expression (used in reverse URL resolving).\nUsed internally by Django 