. '+0200', '-0430'.\n\nIf timezone information is not available, return an empty string.", "start_line": 130, "end_line": 143, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "P", "qualified_name": "P", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Time, in 12-hour hours, minutes and 'a.m.'/'p.m.', with minutes left\noff if they're zero and the strings 'midnight' and 'noon' if\nappropriate. Examples: '1 a.m.', '1:30 p.m.', 'midnight', 'noon',\n'12:30 p.m.' Proprietary extension.", "start_line": 145, "end_line": 156, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "s", "qualified_name": "s", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Seconds; i.e. '00' to '59'", "start_line": 158, "end_line": 160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "T", "qualified_name": "T", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Time zone of this machine; e.g. 'EST' or 'MDT'.\n\nIf timezone information is not available, return an empty string.", "start_line": 162, "end_line": 171, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "u", "qualified_name": "u", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Microseconds; i.e. '000000' to '999999'", "start_line": 173, "end_line": 175, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Z", "qualified_name": "Z", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Time zone offset in seconds (i.e. '-43200' to '43200'). The offset for\ntimezones west of UTC is always negative, and for those east of UTC is\nalways positive.\n\nIf timezone information is not available, return an empty string.", "start_line": 177, "end_line": 195, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "b", "qualified_name": "b", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Month, textual, 3 letters, lowercase; e.g. 'jan'", "start_line": 199, "end_line": 201, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "c", "qualified_name": "c", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "ISO 8601 Format\nExample : '2008-01-02T10:30:00.000123'", 