 "min_y", "max_x", "max_y", "ur", "ll", "tuple", "wkt"], "docstring": "The Envelope object is a C structure that contains the minimum and\nmaximum X, Y coordinates for a rectangle bounding box. The naming\nof the variables is compatible with the OGR Envelope structure.", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 205}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "The GDAL/OGR library uses an Envelope structure to hold the bounding\nbox information for a geometry. The envelope (bounding box) contains\ntwo pairs of coordinates, one for the lower left coordinate and one\nfor the upper right coordinate:\n\n                          +----------o Upper right; (max_x, max_y)\n                          |          |\n                          |          |\n                          |          |\nLower left (min_x, min_y) o----------+", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "django/contrib/gis/gdal/geomtype.py", "file_hash": "096a9b7b95eda602a204ff0b6e2b1bb5bf28d45b6e21455bdfb11bd368ba4d21", "imports": [{"module": "django.contrib.gis.gdal.error", "names": ["GDALException"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "type_input"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Figure out the correct OGR Type based upon the input.", "start_line": 81, "end_line": 100, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__str__", "qualified_name": "__str__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the value of the name property.", "start_line": 102, "end_line": 104, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 106, "end_line": 107, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__eq__", "qualified_name": "__eq__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Do an equivalence test on the OGR type with the given\nother OGRGeomType, the short-hand string, or the integer.", "start_line": 109, "end_line": 121, "