ding to the given\ntransformation object, which may be an integer SRID, and WKT or\nPROJ string. By default, transform the geometry in-place and return\nnothing. However if the `clone` keyword is set, don't modify the\ngeometry and return a transformed clone in", "start_line": 489, "end_line": 531, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_topology", "qualified_name": "_topology", "args": ["self", "gptr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return Geometry from the given pointer.", "start_line": 534, "end_line": 536, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "boundary", "qualified_name": "boundary", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the boundary as a newly allocated Geometry object.", "start_line": 539, "end_line": 541, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "buffer", "qualified_name": "buffer", "args": ["self", "width", "quadsegs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a geometry that represents all points whose distance from this\nGeometry is less than or equal to distance. Calculations are in the\nSpatial Reference System of this Geometry. The optional third parameter\nsets the number of segment used to approximate a quarter circle\n(defaults to 8). (Text fro", "start_line": 543, "end_line": 551, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "buffer_with_style", "qualified_name": "buffer_with_style", "args": ["self", "width", "quadsegs", "end_cap_style", "join_style", "mitre_limit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Same as buffer() but allows customizing the style of the memoryview.\n\nEnd cap style can be round (1), flat (2), or square (3).\nJoin style can be round (1), mitre (2), or bevel (3).\nMitre ratio limit only affects mitered join style.", "start_line": 553, "end_line": 567, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "centroid", "qualified_name": "centroid", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The centroid is equal to the centroid of the set of component\nGeometrie