gher tolerance => less points). If no\ntolerance provided, defaults to 0.\n\nBy default, don't preserve topology - e.g. polygons can be split,\ncollapse to lines or disappear holes can be created or disappe", "start_line": 616, "end_line": 631, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sym_difference", "qualified_name": "sym_difference", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a set combining the points in this Geometry not in other,\nand the points in other not in this Geometry.", "start_line": 633, "end_line": 638, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unary_union", "qualified_name": "unary_union", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the union of all the elements of this geometry.", "start_line": 641, "end_line": 643, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "union", "qualified_name": "union", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a Geometry representing all the points in this Geometry and\nother.", "start_line": 645, "end_line": 650, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "area", "qualified_name": "area", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the area of the Geometry.", "start_line": 654, "end_line": 656, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "distance", "qualified_name": "distance", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the distance between the closest points on this Geometry\nand the other. Units will be in those of the coordinate system of\nthe Geometry.", "start_line": 658, "end_line": 666, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "extent", "qualified_name": "extent", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the extent of this geometry as a 4-tuple, consisting of\n(xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax).", "start_line": 669, "end_line": 683, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "length", "qualified_name": "length", "args": ["self"], "decorat