g output returned from the given function, and free\nthe string pointer allocated by OGR. The `str_result` keyword\nmay be used when the result is the string pointer, otherwise\nthe OGR error code is assumed. The `offset` keyword may be used\nto extract the string pointer passed in by-ref", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 63, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_envelope", "qualified_name": "check_envelope", "args": ["result", "func", "cargs", "offset"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check a function that returns an OGR Envelope by reference.", "start_line": 70, "end_line": 72, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_geom", "qualified_name": "check_geom", "args": ["result", "func", "cargs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check a function that returns a geometry.", "start_line": 76, "end_line": 86, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_geom_offset", "qualified_name": "check_geom_offset", "args": ["result", "func", "cargs", "offset"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check the geometry at the given offset in the C parameter list.", "start_line": 89, "end_line": 93, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_srs", "qualified_name": "check_srs", "args": ["result", "func", "cargs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 104, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_arg_errcode", "qualified_name": "check_arg_errcode", "args": ["result", "func", "cargs", "cpl"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The error code is returned in the last argument, by reference.\nCheck its value with `check_err` before returning the result.", "start_line": 108, "end_line": 114, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_errcode", "qualified_name": "check_errcode", "args": ["result", "func", "cargs", "cpl"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check the error code returned (c_int).", "start_line": 117, "end_line": 121, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_pointer