el and its parents.\n\nPrivate API intended only to be used by Django itself; get_fields()\ncombined with filtering of field properties is the public API for\nobtaining this list.", "start_line": 600, "end_line": 615, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "related_objects", "qualified_name": "related_objects", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cached_property"], "docstring": "Return all related objects pointing to the current model. The related\nobjects can come from a one-to-one, one-to-many, or many-to-many field\nrelation type.\n\nPrivate API intended only to be used by Django itself; get_fields()\ncombined with filtering of field properties is the public API for\nobtaining", "start_line": 618, "end_line": 638, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_forward_fields_map", "qualified_name": "_forward_fields_map", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cached_property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 641, "end_line": 653, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fields_map", "qualified_name": "fields_map", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cached_property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 656, "end_line": 668, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_field", "qualified_name": "get_field", "args": ["self", "field_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a field instance given the name of a forward or reverse field.", "start_line": 670, "end_line": 695, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_base_chain", "qualified_name": "get_base_chain", "args": ["self", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of parent classes leading to `model` (ordered from\nclosest to most distant ancestor). This has to handle the case where\n`model` is a grandparent or even more distant relation.", "start_line": 697, "end_line": 712, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "all_parents", "qualified_name": "all_parents", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cached_property"], "docstring": "Return all the ancestors