 get_lookup()\nand get_transform().", "start_line": 1414, "end_line": 1458, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "try_transform", "qualified_name": "try_transform", "args": ["self", "lhs", "name", "lookups"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper method for build_lookup(). Try to fetch and initialize\na transform for name parameter from lhs.", "start_line": 1460, "end_line": 1485, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "build_filter", "qualified_name": "build_filter", "args": ["self", "filter_expr", "branch_negated", "current_negated", "can_reuse", "allow_joins", "split_subq", "check_filterable", "summarize", "update_join_types"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Build a WhereNode for a single filter clause but don't add it\nto this Query. Query.add_q() will then add this filter to the where\nNode.\n\nThe 'branch_negated' tells us if the current branch contains any\nnegations. This will be used to determine if subqueries are needed.\n\nThe 'current_negated' is used", "start_line": 1487, "end_line": 1657, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_filter", "qualified_name": "add_filter", "args": ["self", "filter_lhs", "filter_rhs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1659, "end_line": 1660, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_q", "qualified_name": "add_q", "args": ["self", "q_object", "reuse_all"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A preprocessor for the internal _add_q(). Responsible for doing final\njoin promotion.", "start_line": 1662, "end_line": 1683, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "build_where", "qualified_name": "build_where", "args": ["self", "filter_expr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1685, "end_line": 1686, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_where", "qualified_name": "clear_where", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1688, "end_line": 1689, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_add_q", "qualified_name": "_add_q", "args": ["self", "q_object", "used_aliases", "branch_negated", "current_negated", "allow_joins", "split_subq", "check_filterable", "summarize", "update_join_types"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add a Q-object to the current filter.", "start_line": 1691, "end_line": 1730, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_filtered_relation", "qualified_name": "add_filtered_relation", "args": ["self", "filtered_relation", "alias"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1732, "end_line": 1772, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "names_to_path", "qualified_name": "names_to_path", "args": ["self", "names", "opts", "allow_many", "fail_on_missing"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Walk the list of names and turns them into PathInfo tuples. A single\nname in 'names' can generate multiple PathInfos (m2m, for example).\n\n'names' is the path of names to travel, 'opts' is the model Options we\nstart the name resolving from, 'allow_many' is as for setup_joins().\nIf fail_on_missing is ", "start_line": 1774, "end_line": 1888, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "setup_joins", "qualified_name": "setup_joins", "args": ["self", "names", "opts", "alias", "can_reuse", "allow_many"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the necessary table joins for the passage through the fields\ngiven in 'names'. 'opts' is the Options class for the current model\n(which gives the table we are starting from), 'alias' is the alias for\nthe table to start the joining from.\n\nThe 'can_reuse' defines the reverse foreign key joins ", "start_line": 1890, "end_line": 2005, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "trim_joins", "qualified_name": "trim_joins", "args": ["self", "targets", "joins", "path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The 'target' parameter is the final field being joined to, 'joins'\nis the full list of join aliases. The 'path' contain the PathInfos\nused to create the joins.\n\nReturn the final target field and table alias and the new active\njoins.\n\nAlways trim any direct join if the target column is already in the", "start_line": 2007, "end_line": 2037, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_gen_cols", "qualified_name": "_gen_cols", "args": ["cls", "exprs", "include_external", "resolve_refs"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2040, "end_line": 2055, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_gen_col_aliases", "qualified_name": "_gen_col_aliases", "args": ["cls", "exprs"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2058, "end_line": 2059, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "resolve_ref", "qualified_name": "resolve_ref", "args": ["self", "name", "allow_joins", "reuse", "summarize"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2061, "end_line": 2110, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "split_exclude", "qualified_name": "split_exclude", "args": ["self", "filter_expr", "can_reuse", "names_with_path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "When doing an exclude against any kind of N-to-many relation, we need\nto use a subquery. This method constructs the nested query, given the\noriginal exclude filter (filter_expr) and the portion up to the first\nN-to-many relation field.\n\nFor example, if the origin filter is ~Q(child__name='foo'), fil", "start_line": 2112, "end_line": 2179, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_empty", "qualified_name": "set_empty", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2181, "end_line": 2184, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_empty", "qualified_name": "is_empty", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2186, "end_line": 2187, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_limits", "qualified_name": "set_limits", "args": ["self", "low", "high"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Adjust the limits on the rows retrieved. Use low/high to set these,\nas it makes it more Pythonic to read and write. When the SQL query is\ncreated, convert them to the appropriate offset and limit values.\n\nApply any limits passed in here to the existing constraints. Add low\nto the current low value a", "start_line": 2189, "end_line": 2210, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_limits", "qualified_name": "clear_limits", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clear any existing limits.", "start_line": 2212, "end_line": 2214, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_sliced", "qualified_name": "is_sliced", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2217, "end_line": 2218, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_limit_one", "qualified_name": "has_limit_one", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2220, "end_line": 2221, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "can_filter", "qualified_name": "can_filter", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return True if adding filters to this instance is still possible.\n\nTypically, this means no limits or offsets have been put on the\nresults.", "start_line": 2223, "end_line": 2230, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_select_clause", "qualified_name": "clear_select_clause", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove all fields from SELECT clause.", "start_line": 2232, "end_line": 2239, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_select_fields", "qualified_name": "clear_select_fields", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clear the list of fields to select (but not extra_select columns).\nSome queryset types completely replace any existing list of select\ncolumns.", "start_line": 2241, "end_line": 2249, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_select_col", "qualified_name": "add_select_col", "args": ["self", "col", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2251, "end_line": 2254, "is_async": fa