turn the SQL string and list of\nparameters.\n\nIf 'with_limits' is False, any limit/offset information is not included\nin the query.", "start_line": 756, "end_line": 981, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_default_columns", "qualified_name": "get_default_columns", "args": ["self", "select_mask", "start_alias", "opts", "from_parent"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the default columns for selecting every field in the base\nmodel. Will sometimes be called to pull in related models (e.g. via\nselect_related), in which case \"opts\" and \"start_alias\" will be given\nto provide a starting point for the traversal.\n\nReturn a list of strings, quoted appropriately f", "start_line": 983, "end_line": 1032, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_distinct", "qualified_name": "get_distinct", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a quoted list of fields to use in DISTINCT ON part of the query.\n\nThis method can alter the tables in the query, and thus it must be\ncalled before get_from_clause().", "start_line": 1034, "end_line": 1058, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "find_ordering_name", "qualified_name": "find_ordering_name", "args": ["self", "name", "opts", "alias", "default_order", "already_seen"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the table alias (the name might be ambiguous, the alias will\nnot be) and column name for ordering by the given 'name' parameter.\nThe 'name' is of the form 'field1__field2__...__fieldN'.", "start_line": 1060, "end_line": 1123, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_setup_joins", "qualified_name": "_setup_joins", "args": ["self", "pieces", "opts", "alias"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper method for get_order_by() and get_distinct().\n\nget_ordering() and get_distinct() must produce same target columns on\nsame input, as the prefixes of get_ordering() and get_distinct() must\nmatch. Executing SQL where this is not true is an error.", "start_line": 1125, "end_line": 1138, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_from_clause", "qualified_name": "get_from_clause", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of strings that are joined together to go after the\n\"FROM\" part of the query, as well as a list any extra parameters that\nneed to be included. Subclasses, can override this to create a\nfrom-clause via a \"select\".\n\nThis should only be called after any SQL construction methods that\nmight", "start_line": 1140, "end_line": 1172, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_related_selections", "qualified_name": "get_related_selections", "args": ["self", "select", "select_mask", "opts", "root_alias", "cur_depth", "requested", "restricted"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Fill in the information needed for a select_related query. The current\ndepth is measured as the number of connections away from the root model\n(for example, cur_depth=1 means we are looking at models with direct\nconnections to the root model).", "start_line": 1174, "end_line": 1405, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_select_for_update_of_arguments", "qualified_name": "get_select_for_update_of_arguments", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a quoted list of arguments for the SELECT FOR UPDATE OF part of\nthe query.", "start_line": 1407, "end_line": 1511, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_converters", "qualified_name": "get_converters", "args": ["self", "expressions"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1513, "end_line": 1533, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "apply_converters", "qualified_name": "apply_converters", "args": ["self", "rows", "converters"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1535, "end_line": 1544, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_composite_fields", "qualified_name": "has_composite_fields", "args": ["self", "expressions"], "decorators": [], "docstring":