n a translation object in the default 'django' domain.", "start_line": 289, "end_line": 295, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "activate", "qualified_name": "activate", "args": ["language"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Fetch the translation object for a given language and install it as the\ncurrent translation object for the current thread.", "start_line": 298, "end_line": 305, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "deactivate", "qualified_name": "deactivate", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Uninstall the active translation object so that further _() calls resolve\nto the default translation object.", "start_line": 308, "end_line": 314, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "deactivate_all", "qualified_name": "deactivate_all", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make the active translation object a NullTranslations() instance. This is\nuseful when we want delayed translations to appear as the original string\nfor some reason.", "start_line": 317, "end_line": 324, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_language", "qualified_name": "get_language", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the currently selected language.", "start_line": 327, "end_line": 337, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_language_bidi", "qualified_name": "get_language_bidi", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return selected language's BiDi layout.\n\n* False = left-to-right layout\n* True = right-to-left layout", "start_line": 340, "end_line": 352, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "catalog", "qualified_name": "catalog", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the current active catalog for further processing.\nThis can be used if you need to modify the catalog or want to access the\nwhole message catalog instead of just translating one string.", "start_line": 355, "end_line": 368, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "gettext", "qualified_name": "gettext", "args": ["message"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Translate the 'message' string. It uses the current thread to find the\ntranslation object to use. If no current translation is activated, the\nmessage will be run through the default translation object.", "start_line": 371, "end_line": 394, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pgettext", "qualified_name": "pgettext", "args": ["context", "message"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 397, "end_line": 405, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "gettext_noop", "qualified_name": "gettext_noop", "args": ["message"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Mark strings for translation but don't translate them now. This can be\nused to store strings in global variables that should stay in the base\nlanguage (because they might be used externally) and will be translated\nlater.", "start_line": 408, "end_line": 415, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "do_ntranslate", "qualified_name": "do_ntranslate", "args": ["singular", "plural", "number", "translation_function"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 418, "end_line": 426, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ngettext", "qualified_name": "ngettext", "args": ["singular", "plural", "number"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a string of the translation of either the singular or plural,\nbased on the number.", "start_line": 429, "end_line": 434, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "npgettext", "qualified_name": "npgettext", "args": ["context", "singular", "plural", "number"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 437, "end_line": 447, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "all_locale_paths", "qualified_name": "all_locale_paths", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of paths to user-provides languages files.", "start_line": 450, "end_line": 462, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_for_language", "qualified_name": "check_for_language", "args": ["lang_code"], "decorators": ["functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1000)"], "docstring": "Check whether there is a global language file for the given language\ncode. This is used to decide whether a user-provided language is\navailable.\n\nlru_cache should have a maxsize to prevent from memory exhaustion attacks,\nas the provided language codes are taken from the HTTP request. See also\n<https", "start_line": 466, "end_line": 482, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_languages", "qualified_name": "get_languages", "args": [], "decorators": ["functools.lru_cache"], "docstring": "Cache of settings.LANGUAGES in a dictionary for easy lookups by key.\nConvert keys to lowercase as they should be treated as case-insensitive.", "start_line": 486, "end_line": 491, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_supported_language_variant", "qualified_name": "get_supported_language_variant", "args": ["lang_code", "strict"], "decorators": ["functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1000)"], "docstring": "Return the language code that's listed in supported languages, possibly\nselecting a more generic variant. Raise LookupError if nothing is found.\n\nIf `strict` is False (the default), look for a country-specific variant\nwhen neither the language code nor its generic variant is found.\n\nThe language cod", "start_line": 495, "end_line": 544, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_language_from_path", "qualified_name": "get_language_from_path", "args": ["path", "strict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the language code if there's a valid language code found in `path`.\n\nIf `strict` is False (the default), look for a country-specific variant\nwhen neither the language code nor its generic variant is found.", "start_line": 547, "end_line": 561, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_language_from_request", "qualified_name": "get_language_from_request", "args": ["request", "check_path"], "decorators": [], "docstr