le we support it only in cases where\nwe can detect a content length from the response. This should be doable\nfor all simple views and streaming responses where an iterable with\nlength of one is passed. T", "start_line": 194, "end_line": 229, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_keep_alive_on_connection_with_content_length", "qualified_name": "test_keep_alive_on_connection_with_content_length", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "See `test_closes_connection_without_content_length` for details. This\nis a follow up test, which ensure that we do not close the connection\nif not needed, hence allowing us to take advantage of keep-alive.", "start_line": 231, "end_line": 254, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_keep_alive_connection_clears_previous_request_data", "qualified_name": "test_keep_alive_connection_clears_previous_request_data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 256, "end_line": 274, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_404", "qualified_name": "test_404", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 276, "end_line": 280, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_view", "qualified_name": "test_view", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 282, "end_line": 284, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_static_files", "qualified_name": "test_static_files", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 286, "end_line": 288, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_no_collectstatic_emulation", "qualified_name": "test_no_collectstatic_emulation", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "LiveServerTestCase reports a 404 status code when HTTP client\ntries to access a static file that isn't explicitly put under\nSTATIC_ROOT.", "start_line": 290, "end_line": 299, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_media_files", "qualified_name": "